Remove a duplicated worker->current_at store in process_one_work().

7.3.4-zen1 mis-merged this line outside the unbraced `if (worker->task)`,
so it runs unconditionally and NULL-derefs (CR2 0x138) for BH workers,
which have no task. Panics at boot via bh_worker -> tasklet_action.

Identical to the v7.3.4-zen1...v7.3.4-zen2 diff of kernel/workqueue.c
(zen-kernel commit ba87bc0, merged in d0c3b48).
https://github.com/zen-kernel/zen-kernel/issues/425

--- a/kernel/workqueue.c
+++ b/kernel/workqueue.c
@@ -3329,7 +3329,6 @@
 		worker->current_at = worker->task->sched_time;
 #else
 		worker->current_at = READ_ONCE(worker->task->se.sum_exec_runtime);
-		worker->current_at = worker->task->se.sum_exec_runtime;
 #endif
 	worker->current_start = jiffies;
 	work_data = *work_data_bits(work);
